1
00:00:05,870 --> 00:00:10,790
 High above Collioure, where the last foothills of the Albères plunge into the Mediterranean,

2
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:14,150
 stands a discreet witness to French military history.

3
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:15,670
 The Taillefer battery.

4
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:20,270
 Perched nearly 500 m up on the famous ridge road,

5
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:27,550
 this fortification now offers one of the most spectacular panoramas of the Côte Vermeille, taking in at a glance

6
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:31,950
 the Roussillon plain, the terraced vineyards, and the marine horizon.

7
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:37,470
 Yet at the end of the 19th century, this was no time for contemplation.

8
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,990
 We are in the 1880s, under the Third Republic.

9
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:46,030
 France, marked by the defeat of 1870,

10
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:52,430
 sets out to lock down its borders with the vast defensive system devised by General Séré de

11
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:52,950
 Rivières.

12
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:57,270
 The strategic port of Port-Vendres and the bay of Collioure

13
00:00:57,590 --> 00:01:02,390
 must be protected against any threat from the sea or from the Spanish border so

14
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:03,110
 close by.

15
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:11,340
It is in this context that the Taillefer battery is built between 1883 and 1886.

16
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:16,260
Unlike the old Vauban citadels, with high walls visible from afar,

17
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:20,140
this fortification adapts to the advances of modern artillery.

18
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:25,020
The work is semi-buried, following the steep relief of the mountain.

19
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:28,910
 These thick walls of dry stone and masonry

20
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:31,990
 are covered with earth to absorb the impact of shells

21
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:34,230
 and blend into the mineral landscape.

22
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:41,030
 From this promontory, the gunners watch over the Ravaner valley in particular and cross their fire

23
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:44,030
 with neighboring works: the Galline battery,

24
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,310
 the Batterie des 500, or again the Madeloc tower,

25
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:50,910
 raised higher at the same period to serve as an observation post.

26
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:57,790
 Just below, a barracks housed the garrison charged with watching over this isolated sector,

27
00:01:58,030 --> 00:01:59,310
 swept by the tramontane.

28
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:06,390
 Irony of history: the lightning-fast evolution of weaponry would soon make these fortifications obsolete;

29
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:13,110
 the invention of the torpedo shell and high explosives from the late 1880s

30
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:18,470
 weaken traditional masonry, gradually condemning the battery to military abandonment.

31
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:24,820
 Today, the silence of the cannons has given way to calm and craftsmanship.

32
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,140
 Far from being a mere ruin frozen in the past,

33
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,500
 the Taillefer battery has found a second life.

34
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:35,220
 Carefully restored, it now houses workshops of artisan craftspeople,

35
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:38,260
 including a wood turner and a knifemaker,

36
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:42,940
 while its former barracks welcomes hikers in search of authenticity.

37
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:48,320
 From defensive bastion to peaceful refuge open to the sea,

38
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:52,960
 the Taillefer battery perfectly embodies the soul of the Côte Vermeille,

39
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:57,840
 a place where stone, history, and nature converse facing the infinity of the Mediterranean.
